lling and Coding: MolDX: Molecular Diagnostic Tests (MDT) A57772 and Billing and Coding: MolDX: Testing of Multiple Genes A57880 Regarding BCR-ABL1 testing &ndash; Refer to Billing and Coding: MolDX: BCR-ABL A55233 for BCR-ABL1 testing","4":"Immunoglobulin and T cell receptor gene rearrangement analysis"},"covered":{"1":"The following ICD-10 codes can be used with MRD tests for the purpose of diagnosing disease progression, recurrence, or relapse.","2":"The following diagnoses are appropriate for the CLONOSEQ &reg; test.","3":"Refer also to Billing and Coding: MolDX: Molecular Diagnostic Tests (MDT) A57772 and Billing and Coding: MolDX: Testing of Multiple Genes A57880. For BCR-ABL1 testing - Refer to Billing and Coding: MolDX: BCR-ABL A55233 for BCR-ABL1 testing. Note: Though BCR-ABL1 may be present in other malignancies, for the purpose of MRD testing, single-gene testing of BCR-ABL1 is limited to CML and ALL. MRD testing with NPM1 and PML-RARA is appropriate in Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia (APL). MRD testing is also appropriate in RUNX1-RUNX1T1, CBFB-MYH11, and NPM-1 mutated Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML).","4":"The following diagnoses are appropriate for MRD testing with Immunoglobulin (Ig) and/or T-cell receptor (TCR) gene rearrangement analysis."},"noncovered":{}}}]